      "title": "Replacement is broader than cancellation",
      "narration": "Marcus is offered a new life policy. He plans to reduce his existing policy to paid-up coverage so he can afford the new premium. That can be a replacement even though the old policy is not completely canceled. Maryland's definition includes specified reductions, surrenders, lapses and other changes caused by buying new coverage. The test concerns what the proposing producer knows or should know about the transaction. Start by asking what existing coverage the applicant has and exactly how the new purchase will affect it.",
