      "title": "The producer documents the facts",
      "narration": "For a covered application, the applicant and producer sign a statement about existing life insurance or annuities. If existing coverage is present, the producer presents the replacement notice no later than taking the application and reads it unless the applicant declines that reading. The notice is signed and left with the applicant. It identifies the affected contracts and whether each is replaced or used for financing. Required sales materials also go to the applicant and the insurer. Do not wait until delivery to discover an undisclosed replacement.",
